      "instance_name": "misogyny",
      "label": "Misogyny",
      "description": "The meme may implicitly reference the stereotype that women are overly focused on appearance and beauty rituals, which can be seen as a form of misogyny. The image of a woman performing a skincare task, framed as 'the proper way,' can be interpreted as reinforcing societal expectations that women are primarily concerned with their appearance, which is a common trope in misogynistic stereotypes.",
